To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Maximum number of users allowed by OSF-USR license PAK
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079044115858

Thanks to:

  Martin Moore <martin@decatl.alf.dec.com>
  Serguei Patchkovskii <patchkov@ucalgary.ca>
   Lawrence Decker <ldecker@pbchcd.state.fl.us>
  Stephen LaBelle <labelles@mscd.edu>
   Jim Bostwick <Jim_Bostwick@cargill.com>
   Peter Stern <peter@chemphys.weizmann.ac.il>
   Matt J. L. Goebel" <goebel@emunix.emich.edu>

for their responses.

Things to look for:

There's a bug in the license manager that shows up with installupdates.
Bug with X, xdm logins.
Must re-install license pak after a fresh OS install.
Use command 'lmf list full for OSF-USR' for more info.
100 user license units = 1 user.
Are you just hitting your license max?

The last three items solved it for me. I didn't know we really had a max
# of users allowed or how to tell from the license. We were at our
licensed limit.


Thanks again.


