To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: {Final summary] terminal disabled -see account administrator
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079044115770

Hi Managers,

Although several friends found the problem could have been generated
by the t_failures field in the tcb ttys database, this was not the
case since 

# /tcb/bin/edauth -g -d t console

produced 

console:\
        :t_devname=console:t_uid=xxxxxxxx:t_logtime#929125826:chkent:

and no t_failures field appear. The solution came by digging a little our
list archives. In a message posted on the same problem in 12/09/96 someone
mentioned using /usr/tcb/bin/dxdevices to fix this kind of trouble. So
I login from a x-terminal as root and run dxdevices. I found the console
login timeout field was zeroed. Changed that to 60 sec and now the console
is working properly again.

Regards,

	Oyanarte Portilho
	Institute of Physics
	University of Brasilia, Brazil
	

