Subject: summary: dec/unix 4.0d lpd debug messages
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079044115766

Hi Group,
     Thanks to Alan Davis - Davis@Tessco.Com

Lpd is now logging messages using syslogd. I've asked Compaq and it's a
feature :-)

You can control how much detail gets logged using normal syslog.conf
entries.

Modify the lpr facility in /etc/syslog.conf to set the severity level to
log. The default is lpr.debug. Here's mine :

lpr.info                /var/adm/syslog.dated/lpr.log

