Hello,
	Original post is below about adding a second CPU to an AS1200.  Thanks to:
Rodrigo Poblete (immediate response)
Shane Feeley
Phil Rand (get the SMP license)
	It was 3 steps:
1)	physically install the card.  Have to remove one of the memory rises first.
2)	update firmware.  >>>boot dka500, list, update, verify.  I had 2 inputs, one
 said before install, one said after.
3)	install the second OSF-BASE license.  It requires one OSF-BASE license for
each CPU, the 1st for the primary, additional ones are SMP.  Warning, have the
license when installing the CPU.  Compaq Capitol fax's a temporary license pak
seperate from shipping the refurbished board, and then later sends a permanent
license.  There was some delay in the faxing, and it required a call  for it to
 be sent.  Meanwhile, I learned the hard way - the OSF will not allow any users
 other than root to log in when it has an additional cpu without a license.
	Installing the second license took the following steps:
# cd /sbin/it.d/bin		 --may not be necessary
# ./load_usr_pak		--also, may not be necessary, only if default 4 user pak is
corrupt
# lmf
>register			--take you to a vi editor
> reset
>load  0  OSF-BASE  DEC  $authorization_#	--do this if >lmf list shows
OSF-BASE's as enabled and not active, as they should be active.

