From: Jim Turner <jimt () netins ! net>
Date: Thu, 03 Jun 1999 16:41:05 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: ADVFS filesystem reports out of space, but isn't
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079044115538

I was all set to remove the domain and rebuild it.  I decided to
let it sit overnight as it wasn't deathly imperitive to have it 
repaired yesterday...

It's working just fine today.  I am at a complete loss as to what
happened.  Yesterday, it wasn't writable, today... it is.  So, 
instead of summarizing what I did, I'll just report on what I got
for ideas.

Most suggestions after knowing that I did not have defragment installed
were to whack the domain and recreate.  I was also going to up the
extents to make sure that wasn't going to ever be a problem again:

        mkfdmn -x 256 -p 7200 /dev/rz0g usr_domain

vdump to another partition is possible.  The consensus was to send it
to at least another disk, not just another partition of the same disk.

        vdump -0f - /usr | vrestore -xf - -D /temp/space

I apologize if this isn't a typical summary.  I've never had the 
problem resolve itself before... too bad it doesn't happen a little
more often.  Also, many many thanks to the roughly two dozen people that 
gave suggestions.  It was and is very much appreciated.

